§§ `(a) Both directions: the inverse maps, and VN-29's own tests run back into VN-10`

-- The total maps of Section A are the two CONSIDERs over a constructor type: A01/A02 (a party to the claim -> a role
-- in a contract) and A07 (a harm Article 6 limits -> its limit). Their inverses, assumed, not ruled:
--  - a role that concluded the contract, pays, or holds the insured interest is the decree's merged buyer-or-insured,
--    with the premium paid as the role pays it; a designated recipient has no decree party (the decree designates no
--    one); a role with none of the four facts is the injured person (the decree's only party outside the contract
--    other than the insurer, which the forward map sends to the same empty role);
--  - a limit of 150 million is harm to health or life; 100 million, property damage by a car; 50 million, by a
--    two-wheeled motorcycle; any other limit has no Article 6 harm.
GIVEN r IS A `A role in a contract`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A party to the claim`
`the decree's party for the Law's role` r MEANS
    IF     r's `concluded the contract of insurance with an insurer, branch or mutual organisation`
        OR r's `pays the insurance premium`
        OR r's `has property, civil liability, health, life, an obligation or an economic interest insured under the contract`
    THEN JUST `the insurance buyer or the insured`
    ELSE IF r's `was designated by the policyholder or the insured person to receive the insurance money as the contract agrees`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST `the injured person`

GIVEN r IS A `A role in a contract`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A role in a contract`
`the Law's role after the round trip of` r MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decree's party for the Law's role` r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST party THEN JUST (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` party (`a 2024 contract for a vehicle of class` (`a car not used for transport business` 5) `with premium paid` (IF r's `pays the insurance premium` THEN 437000 ELSE 0)))

GIVEN r IS A `A role in a contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` r MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Law's role after the round trip of` r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST r2 THEN     (`Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` r EQUALS `Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` r2)
                      AND (`Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` r EQUALS `Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` r2)
                      AND (`Dieu 4(26): the person is a beneficiary (nguoi thu huong)` r EQUALS `Dieu 4(26): the person is a beneficiary (nguoi thu huong)` r2)

GIVEN conc IS A BOOLEAN
      pays IS A BOOLEAN
      ins  IS A BOOLEAN
      des  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A role in a contract`
`a role with` conc pays ins des MEANS
    `A role in a contract` WITH
        `concluded the contract of insurance with an insurer, branch or mutual organisation` IS conc
        `pays the insurance premium` IS pays
        `has property, civil liability, health, life, an obligation or an economic interest insured under the contract` IS ins
        `was designated by the policyholder or the insured person to receive the insurance money as the contract agrees` IS des

-- (a1) VN-29's own role fixtures (law08-tests-ch1.l4, Dieu 4(24)-(26)) run back into VN-10 and forward again.
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` `a buyer who contracts and pays` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` `a person who contracts but another pays` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` `a person whose life is insured` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` `a designated recipient` EQUALS FALSE

-- (a2) Every role record (16), the same check: the agreeing fragment is the set of records for which it holds.
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the round trip keeps the Law's statuses of` (`a role with` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

-- (a3) From the decree's side: each party, sent to the Law and back, is the party it was only where the forward map is
-- one-to-one. The owner and the buyer-or-insured share a role, and so do the insurer and the injured person.
#ASSERT `the decree's party for the Law's role` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the decree's insurer` `a contract concluded in 2024`) EQUALS JUST `the injured person`
#ASSERT `the decree's party for the Law's role` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract concluded in 2024`) EQUALS JUST `the insurance buyer or the insured`
#ASSERT `the decree's party for the Law's role` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the injured person` `a contract concluded in 2024`) EQUALS JUST `the injured person`
#ASSERT `the decree's party for the Law's role` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the vehicle owner` `a contract concluded in 2024`) EQUALS JUST `the insurance buyer or the insured`

GIVEN l IS A `A liability contract and a claim`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A harm a limit of Article 6 applies to`
`the decree's harm for the Law's limit in` l MEANS
    BRANCH IF l's `limit of liability` EQUALS 150000000 THEN JUST `harm to the health or life of one person`
           IF l's `limit of liability` EQUALS 100000000 THEN JUST (`damage to property in one accident` (`a car not used for transport business` 5))
           IF l's `limit of liability` EQUALS 50000000  THEN JUST (`damage to property in one accident` (`a two-wheeled motorcycle` 150))
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (a4) VN-29's own Dieu 59 fixtures (law08-tests-ch2-property.l4) run back into VN-10: each has a limit of 500 million,
-- which no Article 6 harm has, so none has a preimage and the agreeing fragment of VN-29's Dieu 59 tests is empty.
#ASSERT `the decree's harm for the Law's limit in` `a claim within the term` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the decree's harm for the Law's limit in` `a claim above the limit` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the decree's harm for the Law's limit in` `a claim above the limit with another agreement` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the decree's harm for the Law's limit in` `an act before the term` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (a5) From the decree's side: every harm, owed one dong above its limit, sent to the Law, back, and to the Law again,
-- gives the same total: the inverse recovers the limit though not the vehicle class.
GIVEN h    IS A `A harm a limit of Article 6 applies to`
      owed IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Law's total after the round trip of` h owed MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decree's harm for the Law's limit in` (`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` h owed FALSE)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
